Unlike 3.0, 3.1 doesn't let you throw Mjollnir...

     Unless you are _really_ strong :)  -- 18/** won't do it, only 25 will,
but when you throw it, it returns to your hand!  This is truly devastating,
as you can appreciate-- its effective range seems to be about ten or twelve
squares, and if you miss something (which I have not, to date, managed), it
stops, and comes back!

     You just have to try this to appreciate it-- liches, rust monsters,
anything unpleasant, (gelatinous cubes!) all can be blasted from afar;
granted, I haven't tested a non-rustproofed Mjollnir on a rust monster, so
I'd advise caution, but otherwise, I think that this single ability might
make Mjollnir the single most useful weapon in the game (in my humble opinion).

Oh-- did I mention that Mjollnir does its lightning trick, even when thrown? :)
And be careful throwing heavy things while levitating....

Happy blasting-- and no, this isn't a late April fools post.




